# Munaxa Identity — staging.
#
# Copy to `deploy/.env` (which is gitignored) and fill in. Nothing here is a secret: every value
# below is either a placeholder for Operations to assign, or configuration that is safe in the
# clear. The four real secrets are NOT in this file and never will be — they are mounted as files
# and listed in `deploy/secrets/README.md`.
#
# The distinction matters more than it looks. A secret in this file is a secret in Git the moment
# somebody copies the example instead of the template, and "we'll remember to remove it" is not a
# control.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Operations must assign these. No default is possible and none is offered.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The public hostname the browser sees. One origin serves the portal, the Work API and Identity —
# not for convenience, but because Platform's session cookie carries the __Host- prefix and is
# therefore host-only. See docs/adr/0004-one-origin-separate-services.md.
PUBLIC_HOST=

# The same host as an absolute origin: https://$PUBLIC_HOST
# This exact string becomes the `iss` claim (with /api/auth appended) and Munaxa Work compares it
# character for character. A mismatch is a 401 on every request with nothing in the log to explain
# it, so it is worth setting once and checking twice.
PUBLIC_ORIGIN=

# The signing key's identifier, written into every token header. Convention: identity-<env>-<yyyy-mm>.
# Generated with `pnpm keys:generate`; it must match the `kid` in PLATFORM_AUTH_PUBLIC_KEYS below.
IDENTITY_SIGNING_KID=

# The PUBLIC half of that key, as Munaxa Work needs it. Not a secret — it verifies, it cannot sign.
# Configured rather than fetched because Platform publishes no JWKS endpoint; this is the only
# mechanism there is. A JSON array, so a rotation is two entries and no coordination window.
#   [{"kid":"identity-staging-2026-09","publicKey":"-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----\n…"}]
PLATFORM_AUTH_PUBLIC_KEYS=

# The images the compose file runs. Built and pushed from the Munaxa Work repository.
WORK_API_IMAGE=
WORK_ADMIN_IMAGE=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# From your secret store, into the operator's shell — never into a committed file.
#
# These two are Munaxa Work's, and Work's configuration contract is a plain environment variable:
# it has no `*_FILE` convention, and adding one would be a change to another product for this
# file's convenience. Identity's own secrets are mounted as files instead; see deploy/secrets/.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Work's runtime connection, as its restricted NOBYPASSRLS role. Never the migration owner.
WORK_DATABASE_URL=

# Work's keyed digest for duplicate national-identifier matching. Work refuses its development
# value when NODE_ENV=production, which is the check that stops this being forgotten.
WORK_PII_MATCH_SECRET=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Safe defaults. Change deliberately.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The organisation a sign-in belongs to when the form does not name one. Set it for a staging
# deployment serving a single customer, so nobody has to type a slug they cannot know. Empty means
# every sign-in must name its organisation, which is right for a shared deployment. A convenience
# over an existing row, never a bypass.
IDENTITY_DEFAULT_ORGANISATION=

# Stamped into every log line and reported by /api/auth/health/ready, so a support conversation can
# start from what is actually running rather than from what somebody believes is running.
IDENTITY_VERSION=0.1.0
IDENTITY_BUILD_SHA=
